  "_comment": [
    "Golden OSV-Scanner report used by convert_test.go so conversion tests run",
    "without the osv-scanner binary installed.",
    "",
    "Captured from OSV-Scanner v2.4.0 (`osv-scanner scan source --format json",
    "--recursive`) against testdata/vulnerable-app, then trimmed. Field names and",
    "shapes are verbatim from real output. In particular, verbatim and load-bearing:",
    "  - source.path is ABSOLUTE, unlike Trivy's relative Target.",
    "  - vulnerability.id is GHSA-*, with the CVE in aliases.",
    "  - severity appears only as groups[].max_severity, a CVSS score as a string.",
    "  - one group can hold several ids (the lodash groups do), and an advisory's",
    "    own aliases can name two different CVEs.",
    "Trimmed: details truncated to the first paragraph, references to three, and the",
    "severity/database_specific/published/modified fields dropped as unread.",
    "",
    "The absolute path prefix was rewritten from the capture machine's home",
    "directory to /home/dev/pindrop so the fixture is stable across checkouts.",
    "",
    "Two results are synthetic on purpose: the go.mod result exercises the Go",
    "ecosystem and version vocabulary gap against Trivy, and the requirements.txt",
    "result exercises a scanned manifest with no findings."
